## 1. MCP Dockerfile

Create:

```text
Dockerfile.mcp
```

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim

WORKDIR /app

ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
ENV PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1

COPY requirements.txt .

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

COPY app ./app

EXPOSE 8100

CMD ["uvicorn", "app.mcp.server:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8100"]
```

Your application structure can remain:

```text
ai-python-weather-agent/
├── app/
│   ├── mcp/
│   │   └── server.py
│   ├── tools/
│   │   └── mcp/
│   │       └── weather_tools.py
│   └── ...
├── requirements.txt
├── Dockerfile.mcp
└── helm-mcp/
```

Your current FastMCP application:

```python
app = mcp.streamable_http_app()
```

means the Kubernetes Service simply needs to forward traffic to port `8100`.

