# 7. Ingress

For your MCP endpoint, I would expose:

```text
https://weather-mcp.example.com/mcp
```

Create:

`helm-mcp/templates/ingress.yaml`

```yaml
{{- if .Values.ingress.enabled }}

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress

metadata:
  name: ai-python-weather-mcp

  annotations:
    nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/proxy-read-timeout: "3600"
    nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/proxy-send-timeout: "3600"
    nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/proxy-buffering: "off"

spec:
  ingressClassName: {{ .Values.ingress.className }}

  rules:
    - host: {{ .Values.ingress.host }}

      http:
        paths:
          - path: /mcp
            pathType: Prefix

            backend:
              service:
                name: ai-python-weather-mcp
                port:
                  number: 80

{{- end }}
```

The important settings here are:

```yaml
proxy-read-timeout: "3600"
proxy-send-timeout: "3600"
proxy-buffering: "off"
```

because your MCP transport uses long-lived HTTP/SSE-style communication.

