# 12. One important architecture decision for your MCP

For your current python-project-1st-sep, I would **not** combine MCP with your existing weather API deployment.

Keep:

```text
                     ┌────────────────────────┐
                     │      GKE Cluster       │
                     │                        │
                     │  ┌──────────────────┐  │
Client ──────────────┼─►│ Weather API      │  │
                     │  │ :8000            │  │
                     │  └──────────────────┘  │
                     │                        │
                     │  ┌──────────────────┐  │
n8n / MCP Client ────┼─►│ Weather MCP      │  │
                     │  │ :8100 /mcp       │  │
                     │  └──────────────────┘  │
                     │                        │
                     └────────────────────────┘
```

That gives you independent scaling:

```text
Weather API
    replicas: 3

MCP Server
    replicas: 3
```

and later you can add:

```text
get_weather
get_weather_forecast
get_weather_alerts
get_weather_history
```

without changing the main REST API.

